# .gcloudignore — what `gcloud builds submit` must NOT upload as build context.
#
# Without this file gcloud infers the ignore list from .gitignore, which mostly works but is
# implicit: anything NOT gitignored gets uploaded, including things no image needs (the mock-up
# PNGs, the reports, the workshop text). Being explicit keeps the context small and stops a
# future untracked-but-large directory from silently slowing every build.
#
# What the images actually need:
#   Dockerfile.mcp  → mcp_servers/<group>/, packages/vibeflix-common/
#   Dockerfile.app  → frontend/ (SOURCE — it runs npm ci && npm run build itself), agents/,
#                     packages/vibeflix-common/
#   Dockerfile.agent→ agents/, packages/vibeflix-common/
# Anything outside those trees is safe to exclude.

.git/
.gitignore

# Local Python + Node environments (each hundreds of MB, rebuilt inside the image anyway).
.venv/
.venv-tools/
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
# The app image builds the frontend from source in its own node stage, so a locally-built
# bundle is dead weight — and shipping it risks baking in a stale VITE_DEFAULT_IMAGE.
frontend/dist/

# Seed artefacts that reach the cloud by other means: the mock-ups are uploaded to GCS by
# setup_buckets.sh, and the legal docs by setup_legal_rag.sh. Neither belongs in an image.
deploy/img/
resource/legal/docs/

# Terraform state + plugin caches.
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# Docs, reports and workshop material — read by humans, never by a build.
*.md
docs/
workshop/
eng-report/
deploy/docs/
deploy-vibeflix-skill/

# Local run artefacts.
data/
.claude/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
deploy/agent_identities.json
deploy/.env
